IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il41-nouns`
IMPORT `il41-opinions`

-- TESTS for Chapter A (ss 1 to 5), written from the text (Sefer HaChukim 3550 p. 802) before the modules were run.
-- Hand rules: s 4 binds a written opinion on the existing law, as stating the existing law, on the components of the executive authority; s 5(a)(1) frees a holder of judicial or
-- quasi-judicial power; s 5(a)(2) lets the Government decide that it, or anyone s 4 binds, need not; s 5(c)(1) takes the criminal-law domain out of s 5(a)(2); s 5(c)(2) says the exercise of a
-- statutory power of the Attorney General is not an opinion for ss 4 and 5(a)(2).  The Law commences on 1 January 2027 (s 18).

§ `Tests: Chapter A`

#ASSERT `a body is part of the executive authority` `the Government` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a body is part of the executive authority` `a unit of the executive that is not incorporated` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a body is part of the executive authority` `an incorporated body` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a body is part of the executive authority` `the Knesset` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a body is part of the executive authority` `a holder of judicial or quasi-judicial power` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a body is a court within s 1` `a court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `a body is a court within s 1` `the Government` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `a body is a court within s 1` `a holder of judicial or quasi-judicial power` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `a body is the Minister of s 1` `the Minister of Justice`
#ASSERT NOT (`a body is the Minister of s 1` `a minister`)
#ASSERT `s 3(b) permits an opinion to be given orally` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(b) permits an opinion to be given orally` FALSE)

-- s 4: arguments are: kind, in writing, about the existing law, an exercise of a statutory power, in the criminal-law domain, the Government has decided, the day, the commencement.
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 31 12 2026) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a minister` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a holder of judicial or quasi-judicial power` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a holder of judicial or quasi-judicial power` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `the Knesset` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `an incorporated body` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `the Government` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `the Government` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4 makes the body see the opinion as stating the existing law` `a unit of the executive that is not incorporated` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (Date 2 1 2027) (Date 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `the committee on whose table s 5(b) says the Government lays its decision` FALSE EQUALS `the Constitution, Law and Justice Committee`
#ASSERT `the committee on whose table s 5(b) says the Government lays its decision` TRUE EQUALS `the Foreign Affairs and Defense Committee`
